  "initialization_policy": "Stage 2 precision arm: two gentle joint epochs from the relabelled ConvNeXt-Base checkpoint (weights bit-identical to validated_002304.pt; only its stale EMA validation record was replaced by the re-run of those exact weights, 92.00/92.03). The objective is sharpened exactly where precision was lost: the VFL positive target becomes ((IoU-0.40)/0.60)^2 so a 0.50-IoU near-miss stops being rewarded like a 0.85-IoU box, and the background term is doubled (vfl_negative_weight=2.0) to punish hard negatives. No tensor topology changes, TRAIN-only ignore shield retained, evaluation protocol unchanged. Selection uses P at R>=0.90 rather than min(P,R), so the reported checkpoint is the one that maximises precision while keeping Recall >= 90%.",
